IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpfta-types`

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Part 1 (ss 1 and 2) and the
-- First Schedule.  Source: source/CPFTA2003.txt lines 75 to 253 and 2387 to 2401.
--
-- Section 1 (short title) is inert.  Section 2(1) is a list of definitions; each
-- defined term the Act relies on is a rule here.  Definitions that only point at
-- another Act ("hire-purchase agreement", "motor vehicle", "Small Claims
-- Tribunal") are facts in cpfta-types.l4 and are not rules.

§ `Part 1 -- Preliminary`

§§ `2(1) "supplier"`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'supplier' (a) to (d) and the words of inclusion"
GIVEN s IS A `Supplier Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a supplier` IF
        (     s's `the person acts in the course of the person's business`
          AND (   s's `the person provides goods or services to consumers`
               OR s's `the person manufactures, assembles or produces goods`
               OR s's `the person promotes the use or purchase of goods or services`
               OR s's `the person receives or is entitled to receive money or other consideration as a result of the provision of goods or services to consumers`))
     OR s's `the person is an employee or agent of a person who acts in the course of business and does any of those things`

§§ `2(1) "consumer" and 2(2)`

-- 2(2): an individual who holds himself or herself out as acting exclusively in
-- the course of business is treated as so acting.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Consumer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is treated as acting exclusively in the course of business` IF
        c's `the person acts exclusively in the course of business`
     OR c's `the person holds himself or herself out as acting exclusively in the course of business`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'consumer' (a) and (b)"
GIVEN c IS A `Consumer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a consumer` IF
        c's `the person is an individual`
    AND NOT `the person is treated as acting exclusively in the course of business` c
    AND (   c's `the person receives or has the right to receive goods or services from a supplier`
         OR c's `the person has a legal obligation to pay a supplier for goods or services that have been or are to be supplied to another individual`)

§§ `2(1) "financial product" and "financial services"; 2(3)`

-- 2(3): a person regulated under a written law includes a person exempted from
-- being licensed, approved or regulated under it.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'financial product' (a) to (c) and s 2(3)"
GIVEN r IS A `Regulated Thing Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is regulated as a financial matter` IF
        r's `the thing is regulated, or supplied by a person regulated, under a written law administered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
     OR r's `the thing is regulated, or supplied by a person regulated, under the Commodity Trading Act 1992`
     OR r's `the thing is regulated, or supplied by a person regulated, under another written law that the Minister has by order prescribed`
     OR r's `the person supplying the thing is exempted from being licensed, approved or regulated under such a written law`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'financial product'"
GIVEN r IS A `Regulated Thing Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a financial product` IF
    `the thing is regulated as a financial matter` r

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'financial services'"
GIVEN r IS A `Regulated Thing Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is financial services` IF
    `the thing is regulated as a financial matter` r

§§ `2(1) "residential property", "voucher", "goods"`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'residential property'"
GIVEN p IS A `Residential Property Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is residential property` IF
        p's `the thing is a house, flat or other premises`
    AND (   p's `the thing is permitted by a written law to be used as a dwelling house`
         OR p's `the thing is in the course of being constructed`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'voucher'"
GIVEN v IS A `Voucher Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a voucher` IF
        v's `the thing is a document`
    AND (   v's `the document purports to give the holder the right to obtain goods or a service`
         OR v's `the document purports to give the holder the right to obtain goods or a service at a discounted or reduced price`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'goods' (a)(i), (a)(ii), (b), (c)"
GIVEN g IS A `Goods Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is goods` IF
        g's `the thing is personal property, whether tangible or intangible`
     OR g's `the thing is a chattel attached or intended to be attached to real property on or after delivery`
     OR `the thing is a financial product` (g's `regulation of the thing`)
     OR g's `the thing is credit, including credit extended solely on the security of land`
     OR `the thing is residential property` (g's `residential property facts`)
     OR `the thing is a voucher` (g's `voucher facts`)

§§ `2(1) "time share contract", "services"`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'time share rights' and 'time share contract'"
GIVEN t IS A `Time Share Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is a time share contract` IF
        t's `the contract confers or purports to confer on an individual rights to use living accommodation used or intended to be used for leisure by a class of persons all of whom have such rights`
    AND t's `the rights are for a specified or ascertainable period`
    AND NOT t's `the rights arise under a contract of employment`
    AND NOT t's `the rights arise under an insurance policy`
    AND t's `the period during which the rights are exercisable, in years` AT LEAST 3

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'services' (a) to (d)"
GIVEN s IS A `Services Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is services` IF
        s's `the service involves the addition to or maintenance, repair or alteration of goods or residential property`
     OR (    s's `the service is a membership in a club or organisation`
         AND s's `the club or organisation is a business formed to make a profit for its owners`)
     OR (    s's `the service is the right to use time share accommodation under a time share contract`
         AND `the contract is a time share contract` (s's `time share contract`))
     OR (    s's `the service is offered or provided as financial services`
         AND `the service is financial services` (s's `the service is a financial service`))

§§ `2(1) "consumer transaction"; First Schedule`

-- First Schedule para 1(a): the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable
-- property is excluded, "but not including any lease of residential property
-- granted in consideration of rent or any time share contract".  Para 1(b):
-- service under a contract of employment (to avoid doubt).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, First Schedule, paragraph 1(a) and (b)"
GIVEN t IS A `Transaction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction is an excluded transaction` IF
        (    t's `the transaction is the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable property`
         AND NOT (   t's `the transaction is a lease of residential property granted in consideration of rent`
                  OR t's `the transaction is a time share contract`))
     OR t's `the transaction is service provided under a contract of employment`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'consumer transaction' (a) and (b), and the words 'but does not include any transaction specified in the First Schedule'"
GIVEN t IS A `Transaction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction is a consumer transaction` IF
        (   t's `a supplier supplies goods or services to a consumer as a result of a purchase, lease, gift, contest or other arrangement`
         OR t's `a supplier and a consumer have an agreement, made as a result of a purchase, lease, gift, contest or other arrangement, under which the supplier is to supply goods or services to the consumer or to another consumer specified in the agreement`)
    AND NOT `the transaction is an excluded transaction` t

§§ `2(1) "material fact", "motor vehicle sale contract", "specified dispute resolution scheme"`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'material fact'"
GIVEN `the supplier knows or ought reasonably to know that the information would affect the decision of a consumer to enter into a consumer transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information is a material fact` IF
    `the supplier knows or ought reasonably to know that the information would affect the decision of a consumer to enter into a consumer transaction`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'motor vehicle dealer' and 'motor vehicle sale contract'"
GIVEN `the contract is between a consumer and a supplier of motor vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of a motor vehicle to the consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is a motor vehicle sale contract` IF
        `the contract is between a consumer and a supplier of motor vehicles`
    AND `the contract is for the sale of a motor vehicle to the consumer`

-- "specified dispute resolution scheme" is whatever regulations under
-- s 43(2)(k) specify.  No such regulations are an input, so which schemes are
-- specified is not answered here; s 7(11) takes the availability of a scheme as
-- a fact (Regard Facts).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'specified dispute resolution scheme' and s 43(2)(k)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no regulations under section 43(2)(k) specifying a dispute resolution scheme are encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no regulations under section 43(2)(k) specifying a dispute resolution scheme are encoded in this model"

-- "specified body" is a person or body appointed by the Minister under
-- s 8(10); see cpfta-part2-redress.l4, s 8.
